Steps:
[NAV] navigate to {{FRONT_URL}}/sign-in
[ACT] fill email field with {{USER_EMAIL}}
[ACT] fill password field with {{USER_PASSWORD}}
[ACT] click Sign In button
[WAIT] wait for homepage to load
[ASSERT] execute window.dataLayer in console and inspect config event

Test_Data:
url={{FRONT_URL}}
user={{USER_EMAIL}}
password={{USER_PASSWORD}}
an_card=@td(AUTHORIZENET_VISA.number)
an_exp=@td(AUTHORIZENET_VISA.expiry)
an_cvv=@td(AUTHORIZENET_VISA.cvv)

Assertions:
[MATH] the number of home_events = 1 {SPEC}
[STATE] home_events[0][2].item_list_name equals home_list_name {SPEC}
[MATH] home_events[0][2].items.length = cards_home {SPEC}
[MATH] the number of sel_home = 1 {SPEC}
[STATE] sel_home[0][2].item_list_id === 'products_block' and sel_home[0][2].items[0].item_name equals home_card_title (captured before the click) {SPEC}
[MATH] the number of view_a = 1 {BL}
[STATE] view_a[0][2].items[0].item_id equals sku_a (captured from the page) and view_a[0][2].value is greater than 0 {BL}
[MATH] the number of list_a entries with e[2].item_list_id === rec_list_id = 1 {SPEC}
[STATE] that entry's e[2].related_id equals id_a (captured from the product response) and e[2].related_type === 'product' {SPEC}
[MATH] that entry's e[2].items.length = rec_cards {SPEC}
[MATH] the number of sel_a entries with e[2].item_list_id === rec_list_id = 1 {SPEC}
[STATE] that select_item has e[2].related_id equal to id_a and e[2].items[0].item_name equal to rec_card_title (captured before the click) {SPEC}
[MATH] the number of view_b = 1 {SPEC}
[STATE] view_b[0][2].items[0].item_id equals sku_b (captured from the page) and sku_b differs from sku_a {SPEC}
[STATE] every list_b entry has an e[2].related_id different from id_a {SPEC}

Cross_Layer_Checks:
[CONSOLE] no TypeError or JS error on any of the three screens
[NETWORK] the /g/collect requests carry one en=view_item_list per view_item_list in window.dataLayer, one en=select_item per select_item and one en=view_item per view_item {SPEC}
[NETWORK] no 4xx/5xx on /graphql

Assertions:
[MATH] for each products_block container the number of guest_events with e[2].item_list_name equal to the container's data-list-name = 1 {SPEC}
[MATH] for each guest container e[2].items.length = the number of its product cards {SPEC}
[STATE] for each guest event the e[2].items[i].item_name values equal the container's card titles in DOM order {SPEC}
[MATH] for each signed-in container the number of signed_events with e[2].item_list_name equal to the container's data-list-name = 1 {SPEC}
[STATE] for each signed-in event the e[2].items[i].item_name values equal that container's own card titles in DOM order, not the guest container's titles {BL}
[MATH] each signed-in event's e[2].items[i].price = the list price of its product (a number greater than 0) {BL}

[STATE] pdp_events has exactly one entry; e[2].items[0].item_id equals {{anchor_code}} and e[2].items[0].item_name equals {{anchor_name}} {BL}
[STATE] related_events has exactly one entry with e[2].item_list_id === 'related_products', e[2].related_id equal to {{anchor_id}} and e[2].related_type === 'product' {SPEC}
[STATE] related_events[0][2].item_list_name equals related_title + ' ' + {{anchor_name}} {SPEC}
[MATH] related_events[0][2].items.length = {{related_count}} {SPEC}
[STATE] var_events has exactly one entry with e[2].related_id equal to {{var_id}}, e[2].related_type === 'product' and e[2].item_list_name equal to var_title + ' ' + {{var_name}} {SPEC}
[STATE] rec_event e[2].item_list_id equals 'recommended_products_' followed by the block's model, e[2].item_list_name equals rec_title + ' ' + the PDP product name, e[2].related_type === 'product' {SPEC}
[STATE] rb_event e[2].item_list_name equals rb_title and e[2] has no related_id key {SPEC}
[STATE] every item of every captured list event has item_id and item_name non-empty strings and a currency {BL}
[STATE] no captured list event carries a top-level items_skus field {BL}

[MATH] the number of carousel_events = 1 (one impression on the cold load at 1920) {SPEC}
[MATH] the number of grid_events = 1 (one impression on the cold load at 800) {SPEC}
[STATE] each impression event has e[2].related_id equal to {{anchor_id}}, e[2].related_type === 'product' and e[2].item_list_name ending with {{anchor_name}} {SPEC}
[MATH] carousel_events[0][2].items.length = {{related_count}} {SPEC}
[MATH] grid_events[0][2].items.length = grid_cards (the grid reports the cards it renders) {SPEC}
[STATE] every item_id of carousel_events[0][2].items and of grid_events[0][2].items is one of the codes in {{related_codes}} {SPEC}
[MATH] the number of carousel_clicks = 1 and the number of grid_clicks = 1 {SPEC}
[STATE] each select_item has e[2].item_list_id === 'related_products', the same related_id and e[2].items[0].item_name equal to carousel_title (carousel) or grid_title (grid), captured before each click {SPEC}

[MATH] the number of rb_before = 1 {SPEC}
[MATH] rb_before[0][2].items.length = {{rb_max}} {SPEC}
[STATE] the item_id values of rb_before[0][2].items are exactly the codes in {{rb_codes}} {SPEC}
[STATE] rb_before[0][2].item_list_name equals rb_title and rb_before[0][2] has no related_id key {SPEC}
[MATH] the number of rb_after = the number of rb_before (the cart re-render does not re-send the list) {SPEC}

[MATH] the number of var_events_default = 1 {SPEC}
[STATE] var_events_default[0][2].related_id equals {{var_id}} and .related_type === 'product' and .item_list_name ends with {{var_name}} {SPEC}
[MATH] var_events_default[0][2].items.length = var_cards {SPEC}
[MATH] the number of var_events_default[0][2].items entries with a price outside [{{first_price}}, {{last_price}}] = 0 {SPEC}
[MATH] the number of var_clicks = 0 (variations never sent select_item) {SPEC}

[MATH] the number of image_clicks = 0 (arrows and slides are not product links) {SPEC}
[STATE] the URL after the arrow and slide clicks is still the products page (no navigation) {SPEC}
[MATH] the number of title_clicks = 1 {SPEC}
[STATE] title_clicks[0][2].item_list_id === 'products_block' and .items[0].item_name equals card_title (captured before the click) {SPEC}

[MATH] view_n_1 = 1 (first load) {SPEC}
[MATH] view_n_2 = 1 (after the reload) {SPEC}
[MATH] config_n_1 = 1 and config_n_2 = 1 (one config per page load) {BL}
[STATE] config_idx_1 is lower than view_idx_1 {BL}
[STATE] config_idx_2 is lower than view_idx_2 {BL}
[MATH] view_events_1[0][2].value = page_price_1 and view_events_1[0][2].value is greater than 0 {SPEC}
[MATH] view_events_2[0][2].value = page_price_2 and view_events_2[0][2].value is greater than 0 {SPEC}
[STATE] view_events_1[0][2].items[0].item_id and view_events_2[0][2].items[0].item_id both equal {{anchor_code}} {BL}

[MATH] v1 = v0 and v2 = v0 (the refetch and the layout switch send no further view_item) {SPEC}
[MATH] r1 = r0 (the refetch does not re-send the related list) {SPEC}
[MATH] r2 = r0 (the same products in a re-mounted grid are the same entities, no new impression) {SPEC}

[STATE] every entry of lists with e[2].related_id equal to {{anchor_id}} has an e[2].item_list_name ending with {{anchor_name}} and its e[2].items[].item_name equal to a_titles {SPEC}
[STATE] every entry of lists at an index between n_a and n_b has e[2].related_id equal to id_b (captured from the product response) and e[2].items[].item_name contained in b_titles {SPEC}
[STATE] after the Back navigation, views holds a view_item for the anchor (items[0].item_id equals {{anchor_code}}) and lists holds an entry with related_id equal to {{anchor_id}} at an index above n_b {SPEC}

[STATE] no two entries of pages_full carry an identical item_id list (the same set is never sent twice) {HYPOTHESIS}
[STATE] the union of all item_id values in pages_full covers every variation row rendered in the table, with no id reported in more than one event {HYPOTHESIS}
[MATH] the union size of pages_full = the number of rendered variation rows (up to {{var_count}}) {HYPOTHESIS}

[MATH] the number of enter_clicks = 1 {SPEC}
[STATE] enter_clicks[0][2].item_list_id === 'related_products' {SPEC}
[MATH] the number of ctrl_clicks = 1 (a ctrl-click is one click, not two) {SPEC}

[MATH] the number of rb_events = 1 {SPEC}
[STATE] the item_id values of rb_events[0][2].items are exactly the codes in {{rb_codes}}, and none of them is in {{sfl_codes}} or {{cart_codes}} {SPEC}
[MATH] the number of rb_after_more = the number of rb_events ('Show more' sends no view_item_list) {SPEC}
[MATH] the number of sfl_clicks = 1 {SPEC}
[MATH] the number of view_item_list entries with item_list_id 'recently_browsed_products' in sfl_lists = 0 {SPEC}

[MATH] related_ids.length = {{related_count}} and the item_id values are all distinct {SPEC}
[STATE] the item_id values of car_event[2].items are all distinct (a cloned or hidden slide is counted once) {SPEC}
[MATH] the number of slide_clicks = 1 and slide_clicks[0][2].item_list_id === 'products_carousel' {SPEC}

[MATH] the number of car_events = 2 (one per carousel container) {SPEC}
[MATH] the number of car_events entries with e[2].item_list_name === name_carousel_titled = 1 {SPEC}
[MATH] that entry's e[2].items.length = cards_carousel_titled {SPEC}
[STATE] the other car_events entry has no item_list_name key, or it is undefined, never an empty string (name_carousel_untitled is empty) {SPEC}
[MATH] the other entry's e[2].items.length = cards_carousel_untitled {SPEC}
[STATE] the item_id sets of the two events are disjoint {SPEC}
[MATH] the number of car_clicks = 1 and car_clicks[0][2].item_list_id === 'products_carousel' {SPEC}
[STATE] car_clicks[0][2].item_list_name equals name_carousel_titled and car_clicks[0][2].items[0].item_name equals card_title (captured before the click) {SPEC}

[MATH] the number of fav_events = 1 and fav_events[0][2].items.length = fav_cards {SPEC}
[MATH] the number of fav_clicks = 1 and fav_clicks[0][2].item_list_id === 'favorite_products' and fav_clicks[0][2].items[0].item_name equals fav_title (captured before the click) {SPEC}
[MATH] the number of empty_events = 0 (an empty block sends no impression) {SPEC}

[MATH] the number of html_events = 1 and html_events[0][2].items.length = the number of product-card elements {SPEC}
[STATE] items[i].item_id equals the card's data-product-sku, items[i].item_name equals its data-product-name {SPEC}
[MATH] items[i].price = Number(data-product-price) of the card, and Number.isFinite(items[i].price) is true {SPEC}
[MATH] the number of html_clicks = 1 and html_clicks[0][2].items[0].item_name equals the clicked card's data-product-name {SPEC}

[MATH] the number of cat_lists = 1 and the number of cat_clicks = 1 (category stays on its manual call) {SPEC}
[MATH] the number of sd_lists = 1 and the number of sd_clicks = 1 (search dropdown) {SPEC}
[MATH] the number of cmp_lists with e[2].item_list_id === 'compare_products' = 1 {SPEC}
[MATH] the number of cart_clicks = 1 and cart_clicks[0][2].item_list_id === 'cart' {SPEC}
[MATH] the number of wl_lists = 1 (one impression for the list page, no markup duplicate) {SPEC}
[STATE] wl_lists[0][2].item_list_id === 'wishlist' {HYPOTHESIS}
[STATE] wl_lists[0][2].items[0].item_name equals wl_added_title (captured before adding to the list) {SPEC}
[MATH] wl_containers = 0 (the list page renders VcLineItem rows with no product-list container, so markup cannot send) {SPEC}
[MATH] the number of wl_clicks = 1 and wl_clicks[0][2].items[0].item_name equals wl_title (captured before the click) {SPEC}

Steps:
[HTTP] POST {{BACK_URL}}/connect/token grant_type=password username={{ADMIN}} password={{ADMIN_PASSWORD}} scope=offline_access, capture access_token
[HTTP] GET {{BACK_URL}}/api/catalog/barcode-search/store/{{STORE_ID}} Authorization: Bearer <access_token>, capture scannerEnabled and fields as original_settings
[HTTP] PUT {{BACK_URL}}/api/catalog/barcode-search/store/{{STORE_ID}} Authorization: Bearer <access_token> body: {"scannerEnabled": true, "fields": ["gtin"]}
[NAV] {{FRONT_URL}}
[WAIT] the home page is fully loaded (hard reload: the SPA reads store settings once at start)
[NAV] {{FRONT_URL}}/search?barcode={{gtin}}
[WAIT] navigation settles on the product page of {{sku}} (the single hit redirects)
[ACT] in the console read ev('view_item_list') of the /search?barcode= load as list_events
[ACT] in the console read ev('view_item') of the same load as item_events

Assertions:
[STATE] the final URL is the product page {{product_url}} {SPEC}
[MATH] the number of list_events = 0 (the redirect is decided after the search response, so no impression is sent for the result grid) {SPEC}
[MATH] the number of item_events = 1 and item_events[0][2].items[0].item_id equals {{sku}} {SPEC}

[MATH] the number of events = containers = 5 (one impression per marked block, the two below the spacer included without scrolling) {SPEC}
[STATE] the pairs (item_list_id, item_list_name) of the events equal the (data-list-id, data-list-name) of the containers, with item_list_name absent for the untitled carousel {SPEC}
[STATE] each event's items.length equals its container's card count and no item_id appears in two events {SPEC}
[STATE] no event's items[] contains an entry whose item_id is in demo_ids or equals info_id, or whose item_name is in demo_titles or equals info_title (the unmarked demo-product-list and product-info blocks produced no event) {SPEC}
[MATH] the number of clicks = 5 and clicks[i][2].item_list_id equals the list id of the i-th marked container {SPEC}

[MATH] c800 = c1920a (a resize does not re-send the same list) {SPEC}
[MATH] c1920b = c1920a {SPEC}
[MATH] c1920a = 1 {SPEC}

[MATH] the number of lists_390 = 1 and the number of lists_800 = 1 and the number of lists_1920 = 1 (one impression per cold load) {SPEC}
[MATH] lists_390[0][2].items.length = cards_390 {SPEC}
[MATH] lists_800[0][2].items.length = cards_800 {SPEC}
[MATH] lists_1920[0][2].items.length = cards_1920 {SPEC}
[STATE] every item_id of lists_390[0][2].items is one of api_codes_390, and likewise at 800 and 1920 {SPEC}
[MATH] lists_390[0][2].items.length <= the number of api_codes_390, and likewise at 800 and 1920 {SPEC}
